From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t31: add an ALSA/TinyALSA audio transport

The T31 audio I/O currently opens the vendor OSS /dev/dsp device and uses
the Ingenic AMIC ioctls. That device does not exist on the 7.2 mainline
kernel, where the AIC and internal codec are exposed as a normal ALSA
PCM by the ASoC stack.

Add an OPENIMP_T31_ALSA build path that uses tinyalsa for capture and
playback. The IMP API, the frame FIFO, the AEC state and the audio
effects stay above the transport; the OSS path is unchanged for vendor
kernels. The AIC capture is stereo, so the transport captures two
channels and downmixes to the mono IMP frame. AEC needs the OSS playback
reference, so EnableAec fails on this transport until a reference path
is added.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
